    "topic": "Jingle Bells isn't a Christmas song",
    "summary": "Jingle Bells was written by James Lord Pierpont and copyrighted as 'The One Horse Open Sleigh' on September 16, 1857. It has no original connection to Christmas and became associated with winter and Christmas in the 1860s and 1870s; the lyrics never mention Christmas. A plaque in Medford, Massachusetts claims he wrote it there in 1850 at the Simpson Tavern, but where and when he composed it is unsettled. On December 16, 1965, Gemini 6 astronauts Wally Schirra and Tom Stafford played it in space on a smuggled harmonica and sleigh bells.",
    "angle": "A sleigh-ride song that Christmas adopted.",
